## Failures

### LOW: default-variant hover is faint
Location: `Toggle.scss:50-53`. Hover fill vs page 1.04 light; text contrast passes (4.54). Hover is supplementary; consider a stronger fill.

### Fixed: pressed state in normal colors was a barely visible fill - was MEDIUM
Location: `src/components/toggle/Toggle.scss:77-79`.
Before: pressed fill vs page 1.09:1 light, 1.31:1 dark, no border on the default variant.
After: `border-color: var(--sb-toggle-on-border)` (foreground) on both variants. Probe: pressed border vs page 19.80:1 light, 18.97:1 dark (default and outline); unpressed default is transparent, unpressed outline is rgb(115,115,115), so pressed is distinguishable from an unpressed outline toggle by a heavier border and the fill. Screenshots light and dark checked.

### Fixed: focus ring missing on the outline variant - was HIGH
Location: `src/components/toggle/Toggle.scss:66-69`.
Before: outline variant focused by keyboard (light and dark, after the transition) kept `box-shadow: rgba(0,0,0,.05) 0 1px 2px`, no ring, because `:host([variant='outline']) [part='button']` outranked the base `:focus-visible`.
After: the ring is restated at the variant's specificity; probe shows `rgb(115,115,115) 0 0 0 3px` (light) and `rgb(161,161,161) 0 0 0 3px` (dark) on outline, same as default; forced colors 3px solid CanvasText outline.

### Fixed: pressed state lost in forced colors - was HIGH (forced-colors part)
Location: `src/components/toggle/Toggle.scss:81-88`.
Before: pressed and unpressed computed identically under `forced-colors: active` (Canvas bg, CanvasText fg and border), both variants.
After: pressed computes `rgba(5,0,73,.8)` Highlight bg and border with `rgb(255,255,255)` HighlightText (19.04:1); unpressed is Canvas/CanvasText; screenshot confirms. Behavior spec covers it (20/20).

## Verdict
Verdict: ready
Approved-by: Davecelot (2026-11-16)

Focus ring, forced-colors pressed state and the normal-colors pressed cue are fixed and verified (spec 21/21, axe clean, T6 passes). The remaining LOW (faint default hover, supplementary) does not block. Before moving to stable the Figma round must clear D1/D4, including the `toggle.on.border` drift/draw entries.
